---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **「which BTS member is from Busan」에 답하는 자리.** (`/bts-hometowns`)
 *
 * ── 왜 (2026-08-29) ───────────────────────────────────────────
 * 사장님 지시 — 「**인기 검색어는 스타 이름·작품명·노래제목이다. 그 말이 제목과 본문의
 * 위·가운데·끝에 나와야 한다**」.
 * Search Console 실측에서 BTS 고향을 물어본 질의가 **열일곱**, 노출 30회, 자리 3~11위.
 * `/hometowns` 가 그 자리를 잡고 있지만 그 지면은 **123명 전체의 생김새**를 말한다.
 * 손님이 물은 것은 「BTS 중 누구」 하나다 — 곧장 답하는 지면이 없었다.
 *
 * ── 🔴 이 지면이 흐리면 안 되는 것 ────────────────────────────
 * **P19 는 「태어난 곳」이지 「고향」이 아니다.** 병원이 있는 도시가 적히는 일이 흔하다.
 * 그래서 이 지면은 **「born in」이라고만 쓰고 「hometown」이라고 쓰지 않는다.**
 * ⭐ 손님은 「from」이라고 묻는데 우리는 「born in」으로만 답할 수 있다 — 그 «차이»를
 *   지면에 적는 것이 우리 일이다. 물음말을 되돌려 주면서 틀린 확신을 주지 않는다.
 * ⛔ 읽힌 수는 동남아 네 위키백과 조회다 — 한국에서의 인기가 아니다.
 *
 * ⛔ 화면에 한국어를 내지 않는다 — 이 주석은 frontmatter 라 나가지 않는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
/*
 * 🔴 [2026-08-31] 이 지면이 구글에 **«발견만»** 이었다 — 주소는 아는데 «가지러 온 적이 없다».
 *   제목부터 「Which BTS member is from Busan? Jimin and Jungkook」로 물음에 딱 답하는데,
 *   정작 그 물음으로 «색인되어 7위에 뜨는» 기사(`/article/bts-is-not-a-seoul-band`)에서
 *   여기로 오는 링크가 **0개**였다. 안쪽 링크가 딱 하나(`/hometowns`)뿐이었다 — 길이 끊겨 있었다.
 * ⚠ 8/30 밤에 「안쪽 링크는 지렛대가 아니다」라고 적었는데 그것과 다른 이야기다.
 *   그건 작품 지면 104장의 «분포»를 두고 한 말이고, 이건 **한 지면으로 가는 길이 끊긴 것**이다.
 * ⇒ 기사가 여기를 가리키게 했고, 여기서 그 기사를 «받는» 자리를 낸다.
 */
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import KcwMethodLimits from '../../components/KcwMethodLimits.astro';
import KcwShorts from '../../components/KcwShorts.astro';
import data from '../../data/kcw-bts-hometowns.json';

const 부산 = data.byCity.find((c: any) => c.place === 'Busan');
const 대구 = data.byCity.find((c: any) => c.place === 'Daegu');
const 줄 = (m: string[]) => (m.length === 2 ? `${m[0]} and ${m[1]}` : m.join(', '));

const TITLE = `Which BTS member is from Busan? ${부산 ? 줄(부산.members) : ''} — and where the other five were born`;
const DESC = 'Jimin and Jungkook were born in Busan. Suga and V were born in Daegu, J-Hope in '
  + 'Gwangju, RM in Goyang and Jin in Gwacheon. Wikidata records place of birth, which is not the '
  + 'same as a hometown, and this page keeps the two apart. With who else came from each city.';

const 있는것 = data.members.filter((m: any) => m.found).sort((a: any, b: any) => a.order - b.order);
const 없는것 = data.members.filter((m: any) => !m.found);

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: data.byCity.map((c: any) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: `Which BTS member is from ${c.place}?`,
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: `${줄(c.members)} ${c.members.length > 1 ? 'were' : 'was'} born in ${c.place}, `
        + 'according to Wikidata place of birth. Place of birth is not the same as a hometown, '
        + 'and where the two differ this records the birth.',
    },
  })),
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/bts-hometowns">
  <h1>Where each BTS member was born</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    <b>Two of the seven were born in Busan: {부산 ? 줄(부산.members) : '—'}.</b>
    {대구 && <> Two more were born in Daegu: <b>{줄(대구.members)}</b>.</>}
    {' '}The remaining three were born in three different cities. The table below has all seven,
    and then the part that is usually left out: what &ldquo;from&rdquo; is actually recording.
  </p>

  <p class="warn">
    <b>Every figure here is a place of birth, not a hometown.</b> {data.bornNotFrom}
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>All seven, in debut order</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Member</th><th>Born name</th><th>Born in</th>
          <th class="num">Also born there</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {있는것.map((m: any) => (
          <tr>
            <td class="nm"><b>{m.stage}</b></td>
            <td class="fine">{m.birth}</td>
            <td><b>{m.bornIn}</b></td>
            <td class="num">{m.cityTotal > 1 ? m.cityTotal - 1 : '—'}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="fine">
      <b>&ldquo;Also born there&rdquo;</b> counts the other names, out of the
      {' '}{data.peopleInBox} most-read Korean names we track, that Wikidata places in the same
      city. It is a count of people we happen to hold, not a count of everyone from that city.
    </p>
    {없는것.length > 0 && (
      <p class="fine">
        <b>{없는것.length} of the seven are missing from the table.</b>{' '}
        {없는것.map((m: any) => m.stage).join(', ')} &mdash; {없는것[0].whyNot}
      </p>
    )}
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>By city, which is how the question usually comes</h2>
    {data.byCity.map((c: any) => (
      <div class="city">
        <h3>Which BTS member is from {c.place}?</h3>
        <p>
          <b>{줄(c.members)}</b> {c.members.length > 1 ? 'were' : 'was'} born in {c.place}.
          {c.cityTotal > c.members.length ? (
            <> Wikidata places {c.cityTotal - c.members.length} other
            {' '}{c.cityTotal - c.members.length === 1 ? 'name' : 'names'} from our list of
            {' '}{data.peopleInBox} in {c.place} too.</>
          ) : null}
        </p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who else came from the same cities</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Out of the {data.peopleInBox} most-read Korean names we could place on a map. Not a ranking
      of anything &mdash; just the other names our data puts in the same city.
    </p>
    {있는것.filter((m: any) => (m.alsoFromHere ?? []).length > 0).map((m: any) => (
      <p class="also">
        <b>{m.bornIn}</b> <span class="fine">(with {m.stage})</span>:{' '}
        {m.alsoFromHere.map((p: any) => p.name).join(', ')}
      </p>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why we say &ldquo;born in&rdquo; and not &ldquo;from&rdquo;</h2>
    <p>
      People searching this question type &ldquo;from&rdquo;, and we understand what they mean.
      But the only record we can check is Wikidata&rsquo;s place of birth field, and a place of
      birth is frequently the city with the hospital, not the town somebody grew up in. Where
      fans and a database disagree about a member&rsquo;s hometown, the fans are usually right
      and the database is usually recording a delivery room.
    </p>
    <p class="fine">
      So read this page as: <i>this is where the birth was registered.</i> It is a fact about a
      record, not a claim about who anybody is or where they belong. We would rather hand you a
      narrower true thing than a wider one we cannot stand behind.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What this page cannot answer</h2>
    <ul class="cant">
      {data.cannotAnswer.map((c: string) => <li>{c}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <KcwShorts set="btsborn" says={`Fourteen seconds, read aloud: two of the seven were born in Busan and two in Daegu. Wikidata records a place of birth, which is not the same thing as a hometown, and a hospital city is often recorded instead of the town a person grew up in.`} />

  <section>
    <h2>Where to walk from here</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/hometowns">The same map for {data.peopleInBox} Korean names, not just BTS</a> &middot;{' '}
      <a href="/born-abroad">The Korean stars who were not born in Korea</a> &middot;{' '}
      <a href="/member-vs-group">When a member is read about more than the group</a> &middot;{' '}
      <a href="/kpop-attention">Which K-pop names are looked up most</a> &middot;{' '}
      <a href="/own-star">The acts whose members outshine the act</a> &middot;{' '}
      <a href="/debut-age">How old Korean stars were when they debuted</a> &middot;{' '}
      <a href="/star-signs">Birth dates, and what they cluster into</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* ⭐ 이 지면을 가리킨 기사를 «받는» 자리. 없으면 기사는 걸었다고 믿고 화면엔 안 뜬다 */}
  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/bts-hometowns" />

  <KcwMethodLimits
    method={`Place of birth (P19) from Wikidata for each of the seven members, matched by stage name and by born name, then placed with the city's coordinates (P625). Reading figures alongside are lookups on four Southeast Asian Wikipedia editions, ${data.window}. The questions this page answers are not invented: they are the seventeen queries about BTS birthplaces that brought people to this site in the four weeks to 2026-08-26.`}
    limitation={`Place of birth is not a hometown, and this page never calls it one. A hospital city is often recorded instead of the town a person grew up in, so where fans and Wikidata disagree, this page is showing you the record and not the life. Our reading figures measure curiosity on Southeast Asian Wikipedias only — they say nothing about popularity in Korea, and nothing about the cities themselves. Counts of "who else came from here" are limited to the ${data.peopleInBox} most-read Korean names we could place, so they are a sample of our own data and not a census of any city.`}
  />

  <style>
    .lead { font-size: 1.08rem; }
    .warn { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding: .8rem 1rem; margin: 1.4rem 0 2rem;
      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 6%, transparent); }
    .sub { color: var(--muted); font-size: .95rem; margin: .2rem 0 1rem; }
    .fine { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.6; }
    section { margin: 2.4rem 0; }
    .city { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: .8rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .city h3 { margin: 0 0 .2rem; font-size: 1.02rem; }
    .city p { margin: 0; }
    .also { margin: .5rem 0; font-size: .95rem; }
    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .95rem; margin-bottom: .8rem; }
    th, td { padding: .45rem .5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: left;
      vertical-align: baseline; }
    th { font-weight: 600; font-size: .82rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em;
      color: var(--muted); }
    .num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
    .nm { min-width: 6rem; }
    .cant { color: var(--muted); font-size: .92rem; line-height: 1.65; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
    .cant li { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
    @media (max-width: 640px) { table { font-size: .88rem; } }
  </style>
</WikiTip>
